---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/use-cases/winback';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/winback');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/winback');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Design a Shopify winback campaign for lapsed buyers</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">Decide whether a former customer has a relevant reason to return before scheduling another promotion.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 max-w-4xl p-8">
      <h2>Define lapse from purchase context</h2>
      <p>Distinguish a repeatable purchase from a durable item or one-time gift. Use completed order history and the product category to define a review window; a long gap alone does not establish dissatisfaction or intent. Keep customers with unknown history separate so missing data does not masquerade as a deliberate lapse.</p>
      <h2>Choose a reason to reconnect</h2>
      <p>Match the message to something useful: a compatible replacement, a meaningful assortment change or help with an unresolved product question. Do not claim a customer misses the brand or needs a refill. Where no relevant reason exists, reduce contact rather than building a sequence whose only content is progressively larger discounts.</p>
      <h2>Coordinate service and existing commitments</h2>
      <p>Route unresolved complaints to service before a sales pitch. Check whether a subscription, replenishment reminder or recent order already addresses the same need. Re-evaluate queued customers when a delayed purchase arrives. A customer who declines further contact needs an exit, not a new discount branch; have the operator confirm channel eligibility.</p>
      <h2>Evaluate re-entry and offer controls</h2>
      <p>Ask suppliers to demonstrate an explainable lapse rule, purchase cancellation of queued messages, a bounded sequence and a deliberate rule for later re-entry. Record offer eligibility and expiry so a repeated enrollment does not create unintended benefits. Compare the maintenance burden of category-specific rules with a smaller campaign that staff can explain and support.</p>
      <h2>Proposed return-path exercise</h2>
      <p>Queue staff profiles representing a durable purchase, recurring consumable, active subscription and unresolved service issue. Add a new order before send and inspect who exits. This is a proposed exercise, not a test result. For campaign evaluation, compare all assigned eligible customers with a suitable unmessaged group where feasible, including returns and incentive costs. Natural repeat purchases and a seasonal return should not all be credited to the campaign.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
